From c1275e4036e2adb2400fbd628f945c06e62867ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 21:11:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02675/11362] [outer-loop] DeepSeek-V4-Flash-MTP distill:
 fastest (17.8 tok/s, 90% MTP accept) but LESS accurate -- grounded 0/2 vs
 base 1/2

Operator found Jackrong/Qwen3.5-9B-DeepSeek-V4-Flash-MTP-GGUF (5.8GB, reasoning distill + MTP) and asked
if the distill improves accuracy. Result on the 2-game harness (MTP on): FASTER -- 17.78 tok/s, MTP draft
acceptance 89-91% (vs base Qwen3.5-9B-MTP's 67-75%; the distill makes generation more predictable ->
better speculation). BUT grounded 0/2 (base grounds ka59 1/2): /no_think worked (no reasoning channel) but
it inferred the WRONG relation ('editable must match reference pattern' vs the real count rule) and ran
VERBOSE to the 1100-token cap on BOTH games (base grounded ka59 in 427 tok). So the distill trades
accuracy + token-efficiency for raw speed -- wrong direction for the fewest-events-to-a-correct-rule goal.
CAVEAT: 2 games is a noisy sample; the token-cap-on-both signal is consistent (verbosity) but a bigger
benchmark is needed for a decisive accuracy call. Current evidence favors base Qwen3.5-9B-MTP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
